**Confirmed defects (3):**

- **R-01** — `NoteStore.update` (`Attic/Services/NoteStore.swift:212-224`) rebases `inlineOffset` through `NoteTextReplacement.diffing`, which fabricates one span from first to last changed unit. Two edits flanking an attachment in a single autosave collapse the anchor to the diff start and snap it to the earlier paragraph — persisted to every replica. Deterministic repro: body `"one\ntwo\nthree\nfour"`, anchor at 8 ("three"), flush `"one!\ntwo\nthree\nfour!"` → stored offset becomes 0. **Permanent silent misplacement.**
- **R-02** — `NoteTextReplacement.composing` (`NoteInlineAnchor.swift:39-48`) over-covers disjoint edits; `Coordinator.textStorage` and `NoteBodyEditLedger` accept the composed span because their guards check only bounds/length, never interior preservation. Same collapse class, transient at presentation. Enabled by a test that never asserts the equivalence it's named for (`NoteInlineCardsTests.swift:128-168`).
- **R-03** — `cleanOrphans` (`AttachmentFileStore.swift:356-380`) deletes materialization dirs absent from a stale `expected` snapshot with no recency guard, racing in-flight imports via `importFiles`' progress-await suspension (`:106-118`). Reachable in local-only via back-to-back imports; impact bounded to self-healing churn/spurious failure rows since payloads persist.

**Hypotheses (not confirmed):** repair payloads drawn from visible replicas only; `TaskStore.update` converging hidden replicas' attachment data; note-side materialization removal skipping the surviving-reference check; drawer-delete divergence (traced benign — converges via `reconcileWithStore`).

**Historical findings verified repaired, not re-reported:** D1, C3, D2/TP-005, C1, C2, F-04, F-11.

**Limits:** source review only — no build, tests, launch, pointer, or data mutation; race reachability shown by actor-suspension inspection, not timing; CloudKit paths dormant under `ATTIC_LOCAL_ONLY`; line numbers may drift under the implementation worker's ongoing edits.
